WEBVTT

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.660
That's right.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.670
I ordered the treasurer's killing.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.200
But why?

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.480
If we're able to get my son back,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.650
I'll tell you everything that you don't know.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.200
It was ordered by Yoshinobu-sama.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.180
She would've been 
disposed of sooner or later.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.450
But to kill her son, as well...

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.160
I thought I taught you to
 forget how to feel pity.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.690
Right now... you look downright delicious.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:56.700
I remember telling you before 
that I'm not interested.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.080
I'm interested, though.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.870
Just do your job.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.890
<b>Book 1: The Wilderness of Love & Sorrow</b>

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.930
One step closer and I will kill you.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:55.480
<b>Episode 3: Confidential File 614, The Enemy Within</b>

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.420
It's a shame about the treasurer.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.180
What happened to Kyoko-san's body?

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:56.690
It was retrieved.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:00.200
The cleaner will be taking 
care of it, as usual.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:05.480
She vanishes, and life goes 
on like nothing happened.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.250
No major battles breaking out, 
no pillaging, no riots...

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:14.020
Things look perfectly at peace on the 
surface, all thanks to Yoshinobu-sama.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.130
They just don't know 
what's really happening.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:23.110
Even we probably don't 
know the entire truth.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.980
The truth, huh?

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:30.390
I don't think the truth is as important 
as important as our perspective.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.570
You should trust what you can see.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.860
I have to kill Janome.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:48.620
If that's the case, then I'd 
advise dropping the sister act.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.220
That's none of your business.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.710
Sentiment can be cruel, you know.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.480
It's the source of our suffering.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.020
Some things are better off dead.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.190
I got to know the people of 
that temple on a mission.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:29.240
I've already talked to them. 
You can trust them with your "little sister."

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.200
Why would you do this?

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.770
Because it's only a matter of time...

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.850
And once Janome finds out 
you're alive, she'll be in danger.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:43.720
I wouldn't really care if Asahi died.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.810
I'm the same as you, y'know.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:51.140
My sentimental side causes me 
problems, too. So I understand.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:56.560
"I hold the world but as the world, Gratiano—

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.390
a stage where every man must play a part,

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:04.590
and mine a sad one."

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:09.030
That's from the first scene of the first act 
of Shakespeare's <i>The Merchant of Venice</i>.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.320
You need to focus on playing your part.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.290
Arriving

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.290
And I'll play mine.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.060
<i>Get rid of your weakness.</i>

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.380
This is the man who ruined your life.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:44.790
Janome was once a brilliant scientist 
in service to Yoshinobu-sama.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:50.610
But he carried out inhumane experiments 
on children and the elderly.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:54.080
He even went as far as to use
 himself as a test subject.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:00.570
Look at it. These are the side eects 
of the things he's done to himself.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:08.560
As he pursued the secret of immortality 
via cellular genetic modification,

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.760
he found out about your clan, 
and it set him off.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.600
When they refused to cooperate, 
he killed them all...

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:28.430
and took their blood.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.300
Don't cry.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:36.580
If you want revenge, you need to forget 
about the emotions that will hold you back.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.000
Get rid of your weakness.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:50.110
Why did I save that girl?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:52.860
I just don't know...

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:22.960
Asahi?

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:19.030
And the dog Yamazaki-san on 
Third Street has is just so cute!

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.860
She's always showing her belly!

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.360
And when you rub it—

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:23.200
Asahi.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:27.270
You should leave this place.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:30.080
You've healed, haven't you?

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:33.250
Why would you say that?

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:37.280
We should never have lived 
together in the first place.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.440
I killed your parents.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.060
But that's why I...

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:48.240
I've been trying to get you, too, Onee-chan.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.080
Th-Those pickled vegetables 
you're eating could be poisoned!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.550
Wait, are you scared?! 
You're scared I'm gonna kill you!

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:02.980
That's why you want to kick me out!

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.660
When you try to kill me, 
make sure it counts.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.460
Because I won't show any mercy.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.910
Yuki-oneechan...

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.110
My name isn't Yuki.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:24.120
You don't know anything about me, 
and I don't know any more about you.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:32.440
You should go to this temple. 
They've already been told about you.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:37.130
In here is a boat ticket 
and a map to the harbor,

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.880
along with some money.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.760
Use the money if you get into trouble.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.170
But...

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.980
You're free to kill me.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.730
But not until I've done what I need to do.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:54.990
I refuse to let you kill me until then.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.140
That's why you should leave.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.660
And survive until the time comes to kill me.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:17.880
If you're still here when I return, 
then I will kill you myself.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.570
Asahi-chan?

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.760
So? What do you need cleaned?

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:05.680
You.

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:12.010
When we looked into the false assassination 
tip that Hanakaze picked up,

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:13.820
the trail led back to you.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.560
That's ridiculous.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.090
What're you—

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.990
A traitor, bought and paid for.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:24.130
Here's the proof, by the way.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.380
What the hell?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.870
You've been paid a significant 
amount by Janome

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:43.510
on top of selling top-secret information.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.260
Wait, hang on! I've never 
seen this money before!

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.140
You're a terrible liar!

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:57.150
You're going to take us to Janome.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.500
I-I couldn't if I wanted to!

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.290
I-I don't know! I don't know a thing!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.430
I see.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:10.600
In that case, you'll get to enjoy 
Jin Kuzuhara's company all night long.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:12.160
Wait, no...

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:16.610
A fun little torture party!

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.900
First come the nails, of course...

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:21.750
Don't...

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.820
Oh, that really gets the blood pumping.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:27.270
Then there's the tiny hole 
he'll put in your lungs...

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:29.660
And into that hole will go 
some water, drop by drop...

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:30.810
Stop it!

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:36.450
If you'll take us to Janome,

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:40.440
we can give you a painless death.

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:45.470
Guess you're not gonna believe me 
no matter what I say, huh?

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:48.980
All right.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.670
<b>Yamazaki</b>

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:05.340
Would you like to take another home today?

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.350
Onee-chan will be so happy!

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:17.170
Did something happen?

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:22.110
It's okay if you don't want to talk.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:28.010
Such tiny hands...

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:36.900
Everybody alive?

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:38.770
Yes...

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:39.880
Hana?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:51.430
Ow... what the hell was that for?!

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:53.930
I thought you were dead.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.430
What about the cleaner?!

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:01.700
He had a detonator on him.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.440
He used the explosion to get away.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.200
This goes underground to the tunnels.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.340
He won't escape.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.370
If I had to guess, this probably 
exits at that hill in the east.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:25.130
I guess we'll cut him off 
from up here, then.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:32.720
My ankle's twisted from the blast. 
I'll catch up as soon as I can.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.460
Fantastic.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.900
How comfortable is it in there?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:52.990
You've gotta help me! 
I swear, I'm no traitor!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.490
Why not just shoot me and escape?

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:56.980
You are innocent, aren't you?

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:02.750
Think about how liberating 
it'll be to escape all of this.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:07.190
Where am I supposed to run to?

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:09.600
Someplace you'd never get caught.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:17.170
Play your role to its completion.

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:39.370
Huh, I thought you were the cleaner.

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:42.060
I thought you didn't like liars.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.150
He's dead?

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:58.200
Why'd you kill the cleaner?

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:01.170
He took his own life.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:06.090
His coded exchanges with Janome, 
and the record of his payments...

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.820
I've submitted it all.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:11.670
Isn't it a good thing?

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:16.570
It spares you the trouble of having 
to interrogate him, Kuzuhara-san.

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:29.960
I think I want a red coffin.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.320
What about you?

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.000
God, you're boring.

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:48.600
They'll just hire a new cleaner.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:52.740
There's no telling when 
any of us might die, either.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.580
Blue.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.830
A blue one?

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:13.090
But there'll be no coffin 
for me until Janome is in his.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:27.350
And what about tracking down Janome?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:31.520
I thought my mission was 
to track down the traitor—

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:47.150
Do not ever forget where you stand.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:06.720
I see... Then Janome knows about me now?

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:10.490
Yukimura and Hanakaze 
will be visiting you shortly.

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:12.850
What about my son?

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.950
He's been escorted somewhere safe.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.600
He'll be watching the clouds 
pass by in Shimonoseki by now.

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.520
Thank you.

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:26.560
What's this?

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:28.290
A treasure map.

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:33.520
If something happens to me, look for it.

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:36.710
It's the kind of thing that would spell 
the end if it got out in the open.

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.860
"Longing for the sight of a midnight moon"?

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:45.460
An end to the Tokugawa 
regime, Nue... all of it.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:47.310
It's better this way.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:52.620
<b>Yuki</b>

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:38.780
Asahi?!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.700
<b>Yamazaki</b>

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:08.740
Yamazaki...

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:13.040
Yamazaki-san on Third Street gave it to us!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:16.040
So then, the old lady Yamazaki said...

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:35.160
Asahi!

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:39.040
Asahi?!

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:48.850
I seriously hate kids.

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:51.620
They're loud, filthy, and annoying.

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:57.190
I wish they were all dead.

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:32.010
I'm looking forward to 
seeing the siblings reunited.

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:35.410
It's bound to be a touching spectacle!

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:38.670
Right. Everything's unfolding 
according to plan.
